hip-libclc-fma: a fix to intel/llvm v7.1.1, applied by tools/intel_llvm_build.py.

libclc took an amdgcn GPU for one without hardware FMA unless the compiler defined __HAS_FMAF__, which it does
only for a named processor, and the AMD libspirv is built for none.  So sycl::fma (__spirv_ocl_fma) and the
math built on it ran libclc's software FMA on every AMD GPU: a DeltaNet recurrence kernel of the engine took
about 95 us a token on an RX 9060 XT, with its few FMAs a long chain of compares and selects.  Every amdgcn GPU
has v_fma_f32: fixed, only r600 without __HAS_FMAF__ takes the software FMA.
---
diff --git a/libclc/clc/include/clc/math/math.h b/libclc/clc/include/clc/math/math.h
index 2433f38..841cf8d 100644
--- a/libclc/clc/include/clc/math/math.h
+++ b/libclc/clc/include/clc/math/math.h
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 // Part of the LLVM Project, under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions.
 // See https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt for license information.
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
+// Modified 2026 by MistVVK and the XeStrata contributors: amdgcn has hardware FMA (hip-libclc-fma)
 //
 //===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
 
@@ -24,7 +25,9 @@
 #define PNOR 0x100
 #define PINF 0x200
 
-#if (defined __AMDGCN__ || defined __R600__) && !defined __HAS_FMAF__
+// Every amdgcn GPU has v_fma_f32; the libraries built for amdgcn without a processor (the AMD libspirv) do not get
+// __HAS_FMAF__, so the AMD side of this test took the software FMA for every AMD GPU.  r600 only.
+#if defined __R600__ && !defined __HAS_FMAF__
 #define __CLC_HAVE_HW_FMA32() (0)
 #elif defined(CLC_SPIRV)
 bool __attribute__((noinline)) __clc_runtime_has_hw_fma32(void);
